{"id":9863,"artist":"Louis Armstrong","title":"WHAT A WONDERFUL WORLD","lyrics_plain":null,"lyrics_synced":"[00:09.43] I see trees of green, red roses too\n[00:17.58] I see them bloom for me and you.\n[00:23.45] And I think to myself what a wonderful world.\n[00:36.87] I see skies of blue and clouds of white.\n[00:44.14] The bright blessed day, the dark sacred night.\n[00:50.89] And I think to myself what a wonderful world.\n[01:04.79] The colors of the rainbow so pretty in the sky\n[01:11.51] are also on the faces of people going by.\n[01:18.24] I see friends shaking hands saying how do you do.\n[01:26.16] They're really saying I love you.\n[01:31.76] I hear babies crying, I watch them grow.\n[01:39.83] They'll learn much more than I'll ever know.\n[01:45.77] And I think to myself what a wonderful world.\n[01:59.05] Yes I think to myself what a wonderful world.\n","lyrics_synced_enhanced":"[00:00.00] <00:00.00>  <00:00.00>  <00:00.00>  <00:00.00>  <00:00.00>  <00:00.00>  <00:00.00>  <00:09.42> I <00:09.42> I <00:09.97> see <00:09.97> see <00:10.39> trees <00:10.39> trees <00:11.67> of <00:11.67> of <00:12.00> green, <00:12.00> green, <00:14.14> red <00:14.14> red <00:14.92> ro <00:14.92> ro <00:15.15> ses <00:15.15> ses <00:15.47> too <00:15.47> too\n[00:17.57] <00:17.57> I <00:17.57> I <00:18.28> see <00:18.28> see <00:18.53> them <00:18.53> them <00:18.85> bloom <00:18.85> bloom <00:20.20> for <00:20.20> for <00:20.59> me <00:20.59> me <00:21.71> and <00:21.71> and <00:22.27> you. <00:22.27> you\n[00:23.45] <00:23.45> And <00:23.45> And <00:23.71> I <00:23.71> I <00:24.00> think <00:24.00> think <00:24.63> to <00:24.63> to <00:25.18> my <00:25.18> my <00:25.67> self <00:25.67> self <00:28.31> what <00:28.31> what <00:28.85> a <00:28.85> a <00:29.21> won <00:29.21> won <00:29.72> der <00:29.72> der <00:30.33> ful <00:30.33> ful <00:30.88> world. <00:30.88> world.\n[00:36.87] <00:36.87> I <00:36.87> I <00:37.40> see <00:37.40> see <00:37.82> skies <00:37.82> skies 